My old high school rejected my significant gift to establish a finance club where students can propose one trade and the portfolio will sit in 33% SPX 33% IBIT and 33% SGOV to illustrate the differences in returns. 

As we approach end of year, what other math and finance charties do people think are exceptional?

It also included a fully paid trip for all students in the club to the New York stock exchange, and 2+ full college scholarships for exceptional students in the club.

My goal was to establish a sustainable club where the compounded returns would eventually finance itself without the need for additional contributions. 

This model could expand out to other schools to encourage financial literacy that is not currently in school curriculum.

@yackcap It's what I'm passionate about and how I made my fortune.

